@startuml modular_game_engine_overview
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam packageStyle rectangle

title Modular Game Engine — Architecture Overview

package "Application" {
    [Game]
}
package "Static Engine Core" {
    [Engine Core]
}
package "Dynamic Modules" {
    [Physics Module]
    [Renderer Module]
    [Animation Module]
    [Audio Module]
}
package "Engine Subsystems" {
    [ECS / Components]
    [Network Protocol / Transport]
    [Server Runtime]
    [Client Runtime / Game Lib]
}

[Game] --> [Engine Core]

[Engine Core] --> [Physics Module] : discover/load/init/unload
[Engine Core] --> [Renderer Module] : discover/load/init/unload
[Engine Core] --> [Animation Module] : discover/load/init/unload
[Engine Core] --> [Audio Module] : discover/load/init/unload

[Engine Core] --> [ECS / Components]
[Engine Core] --> [Network Protocol / Transport]
[Engine Core] --> [Server Runtime]
[Engine Core] --> [Client Runtime / Game Lib]

[Physics Module] --> [ECS / Components] : components and systems
[Renderer Module] --> [ECS / Components] : components and systems
[Animation Module] --> [ECS / Components] : components and systems
[Audio Module] --> [ECS / Components] : components and systems

note bottom
Detailed views are separate PUML files.
Each detailed view has external-reference stubs,
so it can be rendered independently.
end note
@enduml
